nd  same as i same as myself there are many  many people in cave who are standing up  to the arms  kira rudick a member of the ukrainian  parliament ms rudik you're a very brave  woman we certainly wish you and everyone  in  kiev all the best tonight thank you  thank you and glory to ukraine  well the prime ministers of poland  slovenia and the czech republic have  arrived in kiev by train in what they  are calling a show of solidarity from  ukraine's european  allies  the czech republic's prime minister said  that the visit  is meant to confirm the support of the  entire european union for the  sovereignty and independence of ukraine  eu officials have voiced concern about  this trip and its security risk they've  said that the three leaders are acting  on their own and independently  uk marines president vladimir zelinsky  has signaled that he is ready to accept  his country  will not  join nato ukraine ruling out a future  membership of the western military  alliance was one of vladimir putin's key  demands in the run-up  to the invasion  ukraine is not a member of nato we  understand that we're decent people  we've heard for years that the doors  were open but we also heard that we  could not join that's the truth and it  must be recognized  i'm glad that our people are beginning  to understand this and rely on  themselves and our partners who are  helping us  well that was the ukrainian president  vladimir zielinski there  let's kind of analyze what we just heard  i want to bring in our correspondent  terry schultz she's in brussels it's  good to see you terry i mean those words  from zielinski it's a lot different than  what we've been hearing how significant  is this statement for nato and its  strategy towards russia  you know brent i think it's more  significant for ukraine itself because  as we've been discussing now for a long  time  nato did not intend to admit ukraine in  the very near future and that's why it  was puzzling to everyone why russian  president vladimir putin used this as  one of the excuses for his invasion but  i think it is recognizing the reality of  that for the ukrainian people that the  president was speaking about as for  nato's strategy when it is rejecting  moscow's demands that nato not enlarge  to take in even more members this is not  just ukraine that nato was talking about  this would also um refer to example  georgia which also wants in and and to  any other country that wants to join  nato in the future but i think that this  is president zielinski just readying his  citizens one more time for the fact that  this is not in the near future for them  if ever  earlier this afternoon  the secretary general nato yen  stoltenberg he spoke to reporters at  nato headquarters he talked about the  war in ukraine i want you to take a  listen to part of what he said  for months we have exposed russia's long  list of lies  they claimed they did not plan to invade  ukraine  but they did  they claimed they were withdrawing their  troops  but they sent in even more  they claim to be protecting civilians  but they are killing civilians  now  they are making absurd claims about  biological labs  and chemical weapons in ukraine  this is just another lie  and we are concerned  that moscow could stage  a false flag operation  possibly  including chemical weapons  terry you were at that press conference  analyze for me what we just heard from  stoltenberg  i think the most striking thing brent is  that he used the word lie over and over  i mean this is things that you hear uh  people use in normal conversation but  it's not the kind of stark language you  often hear from diplomats and  politicians and heads of international  organizations and i think that was was  very remarkable today and especially  that lap that last part where  stoltenberg was talking about the fact  that russia has claimed that ukraine has  been manufacturing chemical and  biological weapons this is something we  know that the alliance is increasingly  concerned about that russia may in fact  be readying a chemical attack of its own  and that's why you heard stoltenberg  here today and also in an interview he  did with a newspaper over the weekend  raise these concerns because they're  continuing this this practice of trying  to reveal as much of what they think  russia is planning to do as possible so  that it doesn't come as a surprise so  that it perhaps  serves as some sort of deterrent which  hasn't worked that well but in any case  we understand both from stoltenberg's  words and from officials that we've been  speaking to off the record that this is  something that is of increasing concern  for them they're on very high alert for  a chemical attack and a question about  the language that stoltenberg used today  he said that nato needs to  reset its military  posture  what does he mean by that  you're right to be reading between the  lines on this because uh he mentioned  some things very specifically putting  more troops uh along the eastern flank  more more pre-positioned equipment  holding more and larger exercises  reinforcing naval and air defenses as  well so for one thing this these are all  the the categories that russian  president vladimir putin demanded nato  back away from so they're reminding  putin that everything he's done has just  accomplished the opposite of what he  wanted but there's another thing at work  here brent and that is that there is an  agreement between nato and russia that  nato would not permanently station  troops on the eastern flank that could  be seen as a threat to russia the fact  that they're talking about now in the  long term resetting this posture means  that they they may consider this  agreement the nato-russia founding act  out the window because of what russia  has done so we'll be watching for that  in the future as well all right dw's  terry schultz with the latest tonight  from brussels terry as always  thank you  and here's a look now at more  developments in this war the european  union has launched a fourth round of  sanctions against russia  they ban investments in the russian  energy sector and they also bar luxury  goods exports to russia  and steel imports from the country two  fox news journalists have been killed  after their vehicle came under fire  outside of kiev the same attack also  left a network correspondent wounded  and russia has banned u.s president joe  biden and other top american officials  from entering the country moscow saying  the move is in response to u.s sanctions  you
 

